# Force LF for scripts that are exec'd directly via their shebang line.
# A CRLF shebang (`#!/bin/sh\r`) is read as an interpreter path literally
# ending in \r, which does not exist, so exec fails outright — this is not a
# style preference, it is the difference between a hook running and not
# running at all.
#
# Measured (2026-08-03): with core.autocrlf=true (a common Windows git
# default/installer default) and no .gitattributes, a checkout of this repo
# converts .githooks/* to CRLF on disk even though the committed blobs are
# LF-only. Every `git commit` then fails with
# "fatal: cannot exec '.githooks/pre-commit': No such file or directory"
# under strict POSIX exec (confirmed on WSL2); the gate does not silently
# allow the commit through — it blocks all commits outright, so this is a
# total-breakage bug, not a fail-open.
.githooks/* text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
